# JendCore environment variables (PRODUCTION BUILD)
#
# Committed on purpose: these two values are public and browser-safe.
# Vite inlines every VITE_* value into the client bundle that ships to
# visitors, so they are already visible in the deployed JavaScript.
# The publishable/anon key is bound to Row Level Security policies on the
# Supabase side — it grants no privileged access on its own.
#
# Vercel loads this file during `vite build`, which is how the deployed
# bundle receives its Supabase configuration. Environment Variables set in
# the Vercel project settings take precedence over the values below, so a
# key rotation can be done from the dashboard without editing this file.
#
# NEVER put a service-role key or PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY in this file.

# ─── Supabase (public, browser-safe) ───────────────────────────────
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://ltvjxbydbnneemvadfec.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_DOvmF-zXPrnsXxY1r6FI4Q_E95AzR_M